==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|la|itc-pro|*prijos}}, from {{inh|la|ine-pro|*priHós}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|free}}.

Others suggestions are:
* for ''*prōprīvus'', from {{m|la|prīvus}} or ultimately from this root.
* for ''*prōpatrius'', from {{m|la|prō-}} + {{m|la|pater}}, meaning ''"from one's forefathers"'', taking {{cog|grc|προπάτωρ||forefather}} as comparison.

